{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"202610081431-nether-temple-opus-effort-high","prompting_method_id":"concept-build-free.v0","model_id":"claude-opus-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"concept-free.v1"},"style":{"name":"Nether Temple: The Gilded Ziggurat of the Basalt Deltas","rationale":"A piglin votive ziggurat: a blackstone-brick rim holds a flush lava channel, and a 5-wide grand stair bridges it on axis x=10 to climb a three-course stepped plinth. The 13x13 hall reads as symmetric bays. The corners are L-shaped polished-basalt piers projecting +1, with a notch left open so chains and hanging lanterns can drop from the gold hip corners. Red-nether-brick panels are recessed 1 by leaving the front wall unplaced, with lantern niches recessed a further 1, gilded sills and crimson-trapdoor lintels. Gold pilasters frame a portal of two orders: an outer upside-down-stair arch, then an inner arch at z=6 that reads as a dark mouth. Above run a chiseled frieze with a gold keystone and a gold eave band shown under a 1-block overhang carried on upside-down-stair brackets. The hipped roof steps in one course at a time in inward-facing stairs, with a red window band on the second course and gold hip arrises. The diagonal gold edges climb up into the pavilion's gold corner posts. A gold-raked gable over the portal and a small pavilion gable keep the axis continuous to a warped-wart and shroomlight lantern stage, a gold cap and a blackstone-wall needle. The sides repeat the front with a blind gold-framed niche; the back is plain flush bays. Gold is kept to edges and frames, and soul-fire braziers contrast with the orange moat."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:polished_blackstone_bricks","minecraft:polished_blackstone_brick_stairs","minecraft:polished_blackstone_brick_slab","minecraft:polished_blackstone_wall","minecraft:chiseled_polished_blackstone","minecraft:gilded_blackstone","minecraft:gold_block","minecraft:red_nether_bricks","minecraft:polished_basalt","mi